# $NPM_NAME_RAW

Generated by Supernote Module Generator `$GENERATOR_VERSION` as an
**experimental synchronous JSI C/C++ Module** inside the parent plugin. This
package is not a separate plugin.

**`update` replaces this README. Keep project notes in the parent plugin.**

## Names and call model

| Name | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Package/import | `$NPM_NAME_RAW` |
| JavaScript module | `$MODULE_NAME_RAW` |
| Android namespace | `$NAMESPACE` |
| Returned values | Synchronous; do not use `await` |

## Edit C or C++ here

The complete user-owned source root is:

```text
android/src/main/cpp/
```

`math.cpp`, `text.cpp`, `helpers.c`, and `helpers.h` are live starter code.
Place an export marker immediately before a top-level C++ definition:

```cpp
// @SupernoteExport
double add(double left, double right) {
  return left + right;
}
```

Call the default export synchronously:

```typescript
import $MODULE_NAME_RAW from '$NPM_NAME_RAW';

const total = $MODULE_NAME_RAW.add(20, 22);
```

Supported boundary types are exactly `bool`, `double`, and UTF-8
`std::string` by value, plus `void` returns. C files compile as C23 and may
provide helpers but cannot export. C++/generated bindings compile as C++23.

Every export runs on the JavaScript thread. Do not perform file/network I/O,
waits, locks, long parsing, compression, or unpredictable computation.

## Runtime support warning

Generation and compilation do not prove PluginHost execution. Current official
Supernote documentation does not support direct C/C++ calls from JS/TS, and the
tested enforcing retail configuration blocks execution of the extracted JSI
`.so`. Use this backend only after qualifying the exact target host, linker, and
SELinux policy. See the
[JSI support gates](https://github.com/Ziv-Ink/supernote-module-generator/blob/$DOCUMENTATION_REF/docs/reference/compatibility.md#jsi-has-three-separate-support-gates).

