## Build and continue

From the parent plugin root, run `./buildPlugin.sh` on macOS/Linux or
`.\buildPlugin.ps1` in Windows PowerShell. The parent build regenerates bindings
and writes `build/outputs/plugin.snplg` for the official default; if the
parent's `PluginConfig.json` name differs, use the actual output name. A
successful build still does not prove the host can execute the library.

